Inputs (left): what each side's cable brings in. Outputs (right): what goes out into it.
Drag from an output pin (right edge) to an input pin (left edge) to wire them — chip to chip stays inside the ALU.
Drag a wire off its input pin to move it, or into empty space to remove it. Drag a chip, or the In and Out panels, by its title.
Drag empty space to move the view; the wheel zooms it.
A side a Digital Cable reaches is a bus: wire into a channel's left pin to drive it, out of its right pin to read it; pull the bar at its bottom down for more channels.
Name a Redstone Port (right-click it) and its name shows on the side its cable reaches.ITooltip of the (i) in the ALU screen�Display�§7A 256×256 screen with a GPU, driven over a Digital Cable.
